.TH GUGA 1 "2024" "guga" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
guga \- send notifications to Android via the GuGa server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B guga
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIMESSAGE\fR | \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.br
.B echo
\fI"message"\fR |
.B guga
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B guga
is a command-line notification tool that sends messages to an Android device
via a local GuGa WebSocket server. It supports two modes of operation:
.PP
.B Message mode
sends a plain string as a push notification.
.PP
.B Run mode
executes a command, streams its output to the terminal as normal, then
automatically sends a notification with the exit status, elapsed time,
and last line of output when the command finishes.
.PP
The mode is auto-detected from the arguments, but can be forced explicitly
using \fB\-m\fR or \fB\-r\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-message
Force message mode. All positional arguments are joined into a single string
and sent as a notification. Never executes anything.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-run
Force run mode. Positional arguments are treated as a command to execute.
If a single quoted string is given (e.g. \fB"sleep 5"\fR), it is split into
tokens automatically using shell-like parsing.
.TP
.B \-\-server \fIPORT\fR
GuGa server port to connect to. Default: \fB6769\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Suppress all output from guga itself. The watched command's output still
streams to the terminal normally in run mode.
.TP
.B \-\-title \fILABEL\fR
Optional label included in the notification. Useful when running guga
across multiple machines (e.g. \fB"GPU Server"\fR, \fB"Dev Box"\fR).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH AUTO-DETECTION RULES
When neither \fB\-m\fR nor \fB\-r\fR is given, guga determines the mode as follows:
.IP 1. 4
If stdin is a pipe and no positional args are given \(-> \fBmessage mode\fR.
.IP 2. 4
If there is exactly one positional arg and it is not an executable or file \(-> \fBmessage mode\fR.
.IP 3. 4
Everything else \(-> \fBrun mode\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Message mode
.TP
.B echo "Deploy done" | guga
Send a notification from stdin.
.TP
.B guga "Build finished \[u2705]"
Send a plain string notification.
.TP
.B guga \-m "python train.py"
Force message mode — sends the literal string, does not run anything.
.SS Run mode
.TP
.B guga python train.py \-\-epochs 100
Run a Python script and notify on completion.
.TP
.B guga calc maintenance.cobol
Run a command with arguments. Notification includes elapsed time and last output line.
.TP
.B guga \-r "sleep 5"
Force run mode with a single quoted string (split into tokens automatically).
.TP
.B guga \-r ./deploy.sh \-\-title "Prod Server"
Run a script and label the notification with the server name.
.SS Scripting
.TP
.B guga python train.py \-\-silent \-\-title "GPU"
Run silently — no guga output in the terminal, notification still fires.
.TP
.B make build && guga "Build done" || guga "Build failed"
Use guga inside shell pipelines.
.SH INSTALLATION
.SS Install the script
.nf
chmod +x guga_push.py
sudo ln \-s "$(pwd)/guga_push.py" /usr/local/bin/guga
.fi
.SS Install this man page
.nf
sudo cp guga.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/guga.1
sudo mandb
man guga
.fi
.SH SERVER
.B guga
connects to a local Flask/WebSocket server that relays messages to an Android
device over an end-to-end encrypted WebSocket connection. The server only
accepts connections from localhost on the \fB/send\fR route.
.PP
Start the server before using guga:
.nf
python3 server/server.py
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
In message mode, guga exits \fB0\fR on success, \fB1\fR on failure.
.PP
In run mode, guga exits with the same code as the watched command, so it is
transparent in scripts and Makefiles.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR notify\-send (1)
